1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,340
Hello, everyone!

2
00:00:02,340 --> 00:00:07,400
This is Ria's Slow Korean Podcast.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:10,370
It’s spring, everyone.

4
00:00:10,370 --> 00:00:12,450
Spring has arrived.

5
00:00:12,450 --> 00:00:15,640
It’s April now.

6
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:17,100
April

7
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:21,450
In Korea, April is spring.

8
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:22,770
Spring

9
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:28,580
What comes to mind first when you think of spring?

10
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:31,440
What comes to mind first when you think of spring?

11
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:37,090
For me, it’s flowers! Flowers come to mind.

12
00:00:37,090 --> 00:00:41,860
Flowers are the first thing that comes to mind.

13
00:00:41,860 --> 00:00:46,310
So, what kind of flowers come to mind?

14
00:00:46,310 --> 00:00:56,380
There are so many spring flowers, but right now, two kinds come to mind.

15
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:59,360
Cherry blossoms and forsythia.

16
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:02,180
Cherry blossoms—have you heard of them?

17
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:03,580
Have you heard of them?

18
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:11,150
Cherry blossoms are flowers that are a mix of white and pink.

19
00:01:11,150 --> 00:01:15,200
They bloom very beautifully in the spring.

20
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:17,630
They bloom beautifully.

21
00:01:17,630 --> 00:01:19,070
Forsythia

22
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:21,920
Have you heard of forsythia?

23
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:28,980
Forsythia is a yellow flower.

24
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:37,860
When I think of forsythia, I think of March and the start of a new school year.

25
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:45,410
Cherry blossoms are in April; they feel more like spring.

26
00:01:45,410 --> 00:01:51,910
The weather is warmer in April, too.

27
00:01:51,910 --> 00:01:59,580
The weather is nice, and there are so many flowers blooming—it makes me feel great.

28
00:01:59,580 --> 00:02:01,560
I feel great.

29
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:04,700
But there’s one thing I find a bit disappointing.

30
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:06,590
There’s one thing that’s a bit of a shame.

31
00:02:06,590 --> 00:02:15,200
Cherry blossoms bloom for such a short time and disappear so quickly.

32
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:17,120
They disappear in a flash.

33
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:28,960
That’s why when the cherry blossoms bloom, Koreans think, “I have to enjoy this moment right now.”

34
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:35,680
They look online for places to see the cherry blossoms.

35
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:39,590
They look for places to see the cherry blossoms.

36
00:02:39,590 --> 00:02:45,830
I look for places with lots of beautiful cherry blossoms.

37
00:02:45,830 --> 00:02:50,690
There are even cherry blossom maps in Korea.

38
00:02:50,690 --> 00:02:52,200
Cherry Blossom Map

39
00:02:52,200 --> 00:03:04,250
If you look at this cherry blossom map, you can find places with lots of beautiful cherry blossoms.

40
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:12,120
People go out a lot to see the cherry blossoms.

41
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:14,400
They go out a lot.

42
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:15,640
Parks

43
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:21,300
We take walks in the park and go on picnics.

44
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:22,730
Picnics

45
00:03:22,730 --> 00:03:25,000
We go on picnics.

46
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:31,020
When we go to see the cherry blossoms, there are so many couples.

47
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:37,020
Why are there so many couples in the spring?

48
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:40,070
Why are there so many couples?

49
00:03:40,070 --> 00:03:44,670
There’s a place in Korea called the Han River.

50
00:03:44,670 --> 00:03:47,300
It’s a really famous place, right?

51
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:48,600
The Han River

52
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:52,850
There are tandem bikes here.

53
00:03:52,850 --> 00:03:58,180
People ride these bikes to enjoy the cherry blossoms.

54
00:03:58,180 --> 00:04:02,600
We ride the bikes and enjoy the cherry blossoms.

55
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:04,610
Spring atmosphere

56
00:04:04,610 --> 00:04:07,470
I soak up the spring atmosphere.

57
00:04:07,470 --> 00:04:14,590
Then I eat ramen or order takeout.

58
00:04:14,590 --> 00:04:17,180
I order takeout.

59
00:04:17,180 --> 00:04:25,870
I spread out a picnic blanket under the cherry blossoms and eat.

60
00:04:25,870 --> 00:04:27,520
It’s so nice.

61
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:36,450
There aren’t many days in Korea when the weather is this pleasantly warm.

62
00:04:36,450 --> 00:04:40,830
There aren’t many days that are this pleasantly warm.

63
00:04:40,830 --> 00:04:47,460
In winter, it’s too cold to go outside.

64
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:52,870
In the summer, it’s too hot and humid.

65
00:04:52,870 --> 00:04:56,380
It’s so humid that I can’t go outside.

66
00:04:56,380 --> 00:05:05,700
But I can only spend a lot of time outside in spring and fall.

67
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:15,360
So for us, for Koreans, spring is a very precious time.

68
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:24,850
It’s the season when we can spend quality time outdoors with our loved ones.

69
00:05:24,850 --> 00:05:26,240
Season

70
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:31,300
So, what do I do in the spring?

71
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:40,030
Have I seen many cherry blossoms in my life so far?

72
00:05:40,030 --> 00:05:46,350
Have I been to many cherry blossom festivals or events like that?

73
00:05:46,350 --> 00:05:53,060
To be honest, I haven’t seen many cherry blossoms.

74
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:54,850
I wonder why that is?

75
00:05:54,850 --> 00:05:59,900
There’s a really famous saying in Korea.

76
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:05,410
It’s kind of like a famous joke.

77
00:06:05,410 --> 00:06:10,140
The symbolic meaning of cherry blossoms is midterm exams.

78
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:21,390
If you search for this on the Korean internet, you’ll find the phrase “The symbolic meaning of cherry blossoms is midterm exams.”

79
00:06:21,390 --> 00:06:22,750
Symbolic meaning.

80
00:06:22,750 --> 00:06:26,720
The symbolic meaning of a flower is the significance it holds.

81
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:28,880
The significance a flower holds.

82
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:33,310
What is the original meaning of the cherry blossom?

83
00:06:33,310 --> 00:06:40,060
The original meaning is said to be purity and beauty.

84
00:06:40,060 --> 00:06:45,430
But why are they called midterms?

85
00:06:45,430 --> 00:06:52,010
First of all, what are midterms? They’re exams. Exams.

86
00:06:52,010 --> 00:06:57,750
In Korea, the new school year starts in March.

87
00:06:57,750 --> 00:07:05,380
Since the new school year starts in March, the first exam is taken in April.

88
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:09,230
This is called a midterm exam.

89
00:07:09,230 --> 00:07:13,510
The first exam of the new semester: the midterm exam.

90
00:07:13,510 --> 00:07:20,010
But these midterms all start in April.

91
00:07:20,010 --> 00:07:25,750
Even in college, there are midterms in April.

92
00:07:25,750 --> 00:07:34,180
So, actually, Koreans don’t really have much time to see the cherry blossoms.

93
00:07:34,180 --> 00:07:38,240
It’s fine once you graduate from college.

94
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:40,510
It’s fine once you graduate.

95
00:07:40,510 --> 00:07:47,630
It’s fine once you graduate, but until then, there isn’t much time.

96
00:07:47,630 --> 00:07:50,680
I told you earlier, didn't I?

97
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:57,740
Cherry blossoms are so beautiful, but they fade away so quickly.

98
00:07:57,740 --> 00:08:05,140
But because of midterms, I didn’t get to see these beautiful cherry blossoms very often.

99
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:11,330
That said, I couldn’t just give up on my exams for the sake of the cherry blossoms.

100
00:08:11,330 --> 00:08:16,110
Because exams are just too important.

101
00:08:16,110 --> 00:08:23,230
So I have memories of always feeling a little regretful when I was in school.

102
00:08:23,230 --> 00:08:26,590
I have memories of feeling sad.

103
00:08:26,590 --> 00:08:38,440
The weather was so nice, and when I looked out the window of my classroom, I could see cherry blossoms.

104
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:42,100
But I couldn’t even go outside.

105
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:45,200
I focused solely on my exams.

106
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:48,930
It was the same when I went to college.

107
00:08:48,930 --> 00:09:03,260
So I often thought, “Man, this is so boring. It’s way too boring. When am I ever going to get to really enjoy the cherry blossoms?”

108
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:05,220
How about you guys?

109
00:09:05,220 --> 00:09:12,460
I didn’t know either, but my subscribers told me.

110
00:09:12,460 --> 00:09:14,090
They told me.

111
00:09:14,090 --> 00:09:21,680
I heard that in other countries, the new school year starts in September.

112
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:26,560
So, what do you guys do in the spring?

113
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:32,780
And what are the spring flowers in your country?

114
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,050
Spring flowers

115
00:09:34,050 --> 00:09:45,070
For example, in Korea, the two flowers that immediately come to mind are the forsythia and cherry blossoms I mentioned earlier.

116
00:09:45,070 --> 00:09:46,810
They immediately come to mind!

117
00:09:46,810 --> 00:09:55,230
It seems like it would be hard to see flowers in a country that’s too cold... Is that right?

118
00:09:55,230 --> 00:10:02,080
Also, in hot countries, there seemed to be a lot of flowers like plumeria (Plumeria) and other flowers like that.

119
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:07,440
But I really love this flower.

120
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,490
I really, really love it!

121
00:10:09,490 --> 00:10:18,900
I love summer so much that whenever I see this flower, it immediately reminds me of summer.

122
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:26,820
A while ago, one of my students sent me a photo.

123
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:30,020
They live in the UK.

124
00:10:30,020 --> 00:10:36,570
They sent me this beautiful photo.

125
00:10:36,570 --> 00:10:41,500
I’m not quite sure if these are cherry blossoms.

126
00:10:41,500 --> 00:10:46,660
From what I can see, I think they are cherry blossoms.

127
00:10:46,660 --> 00:10:54,410
Another spring flower I know is called the “jacaranda.”

128
00:10:54,410 --> 00:10:56,040
Jacaranda

129
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:59,590
This is a flower found in Australia.

130
00:10:59,590 --> 00:11:04,620
I don’t really know much about flowers.

131
00:11:04,620 --> 00:11:12,290
But when I went to Australia, I saw this flower for the first time.

132
00:11:12,290 --> 00:11:14,040
I saw it.

133
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:16,610
It was so fascinating.

134
00:11:16,610 --> 00:11:29,410
I used to only know about forsythia and cherry blossoms, so it was fascinating to discover a new spring flower.

135
00:11:29,410 --> 00:11:31,700
It was fascinating.

136
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:39,210
And this flower is uniquely purple.

137
00:11:39,210 --> 00:11:40,700
It’s purple.

138
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:48,260
So when the flowers are all in bloom, it’s full of purple.

139
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:49,620
It’s full of them.

140
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:52,510
It’s so beautiful.

141
00:11:52,510 --> 00:11:57,120
It has a slightly different vibe from cherry blossoms?

142
00:11:57,120 --> 00:12:00,220
It has a slightly different vibe.

143
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:02,450
A different vibe

144
00:12:02,450 --> 00:12:04,740
It has a different vibe.

145
00:12:04,740 --> 00:12:13,950
If you know of any spring flowers like this in your country, please let me know.

146
00:12:13,950 --> 00:12:27,470
Now, finally, I’ll tell you about a song that immediately comes to mind when you think of spring in Korea.

147
00:12:27,470 --> 00:12:31,600
Some of you might already know it.

148
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:36,580
It’s the song called “Cherry Blossom Ending.”

149
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:41,340
This song is really, really famous.

150
00:12:41,340 --> 00:12:46,530
When was this song released?

151
00:12:46,530 --> 00:12:50,400
2012

152
00:12:50,400 --> 00:12:55,250
It was released in 2012.

153
00:12:55,250 --> 00:12:58,400
It’s been over 10 years.

154
00:12:58,400 --> 00:13:00,510
It’s been over 10 years.

155
00:13:00,510 --> 00:13:03,520
Time flies.

156
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:13,410
But even after more than 10 years, this song is still incredibly popular.

157
00:13:13,410 --> 00:13:23,970
As soon as April rolls around and spring arrives, this song immediately climbs the Korean music charts.

158
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:34,270
It’s a really old song, but every spring, it always climbs the Korean music charts.

159
00:13:34,270 --> 00:13:40,150
That’s why Koreans call it the “Cherry Blossom Pension.”

160
00:13:40,150 --> 00:13:42,210
Cherry Blossom Pension

161
00:13:42,210 --> 00:13:45,790
Now, what does “pension” mean?

162
00:13:45,790 --> 00:13:51,300
It’s money you can receive even after you stop working.

163
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:52,470
Money

164
00:13:52,470 --> 00:14:04,670
But since this singer’s song makes it onto the charts every spring, they earn money every year.

165
00:14:04,670 --> 00:14:08,610
They earn money without even working.

166
00:14:08,610 --> 00:14:12,740
That’s why we call it the “cherry blossom pension.”

167
00:14:12,740 --> 00:14:20,460
I can’t play this song because of copyright issues.

168
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:26,110
I can’t play it, but I’ll sing it for you.

169
00:14:26,110 --> 00:14:28,880
A karaoke session out of the blue?

170
00:14:28,880 --> 00:14:36,000
I’ll sing some lyrics that are easier for you to understand.

171
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:39,010
What should I sing?

172
00:14:39,010 --> 00:14:46,010
Just the two of us, holding hands with the one I love,

173
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:52,770
Walking down this unfamiliar street together ♬

174
00:14:52,770 --> 00:15:00,820
Walking down a street where the cherry blossoms are just starting to bloom with the one I love.

175
00:15:00,820 --> 00:15:04,290
Walking with the one I love.

176
00:15:04,290 --> 00:15:07,150
I mentioned this earlier, didn’t I?

177
00:15:07,150 --> 00:15:12,290
I asked why there are so many couples in the spring.

178
00:15:12,290 --> 00:15:18,130
So I think there are a lot of people who feel even lonelier.

179
00:15:18,130 --> 00:15:27,640
Apparently, there are actually a lot of people in Korea who feel more depressed in the spring.

180
00:15:27,640 --> 00:15:31,040
Depressed

181
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:37,220
I really hope you all find happiness this spring.

182
00:15:37,220 --> 00:15:53,230
If you’re feeling a little lonely this spring, try focusing on the spring air rather than the atmosphere on the streets or the people around you.

183
00:15:53,230 --> 00:15:55,720
Just feel the air.

184
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:59,120
Take a breath.

185
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:00,640
Breathe in.

186
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:18,720
When I take the time to slowly savor things like a gentle breeze, the feeling of the wind on my skin, and the scent of flowers, strangely enough, my mind feels a little more at ease.

187
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,420
It makes me feel at ease.

188
00:16:20,420 --> 00:16:29,890
Walk slowly, stop for a moment, and look up at the sky.

189
00:16:29,890 --> 00:16:37,720
Just feeling this way means you’re already enjoying spring to the fullest.

190
00:16:37,720 --> 00:16:45,970
I’ll show you one last cherry blossom photo I took.

191
00:16:45,970 --> 00:16:50,040
It’s a photo I took in front of my house.

192
00:16:50,040 --> 00:16:55,930
But this one is a bit special—it’s cherry blossoms at night.

193
00:16:55,930 --> 00:16:58,100
Cherry blossoms at night.

194
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:02,460
Cherry blossoms are really beautiful at night.

195
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:07,310
The sky is dark, but the cherry blossoms are bright.

196
00:17:07,310 --> 00:17:12,380
That’s why the cherry blossoms stand out even more.

197
00:17:12,380 --> 00:17:13,890
They really catch your eye.

198
00:17:13,890 --> 00:17:19,030
They really catch your eye.

199
00:17:19,030 --> 00:17:27,710
Anyway, I hope you’re enjoying the best season where you live right now.

200
00:17:27,710 --> 00:17:33,960
Thank you for listening to my podcast today!

201
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:37,500
See you next time! Bye :)
